1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:04,003
[microphone feedback]

2
00:00:04,004 --> 00:00:06,006
[♪ opening theme music playing]

3
00:00:40,541 --> 00:00:44,043
FLEX X COP 2

4
00:00:44,044 --> 00:00:46,963
CHARACTERS, PLACES, ORGANIZATIONS,
AND EVENTS IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

5
00:00:46,964 --> 00:00:49,007
ALL CHILD ACTORS AND ANIMALS
FILMED IN A SAFE ENVIRONMENT

6
00:00:52,052 --> 00:00:54,012
[♪ tense, foreboding music playing]

7
00:01:03,355 --> 00:01:05,107
[♪ music increases in tempo]

8
00:01:19,746 --> 00:01:21,206
[♪ music swells]

9
00:01:24,251 --> 00:01:25,376
Bang!

10
00:01:25,377 --> 00:01:26,460
[scoffs]

11
00:01:26,461 --> 00:01:27,587
[♪ music fades]

12
00:01:27,588 --> 00:01:28,713
Whoa.

13
00:01:28,714 --> 00:01:30,089
You didn't even blink.

14
00:01:30,090 --> 00:01:31,382
Huh? [gun clicks]

15
00:01:31,383 --> 00:01:32,509
I saw you flinch.

16
00:01:36,054 --> 00:01:38,098
I'm Jin Isoo, the owner of this place.

17
00:01:38,890 --> 00:01:40,725
And I'm a violent crime detective.

18
00:01:40,726 --> 00:01:42,644
[♪ tense pulsating music playing]

19
00:01:45,897 --> 00:01:47,983
- Is this real?
- It's real.

20
00:01:51,236 --> 00:01:52,486
A rich cop.

21
00:01:52,487 --> 00:01:53,904
[Seongwook scoffs softly]

22
00:01:53,905 --> 00:01:55,282
I really liked this place.

23
00:01:55,991 --> 00:01:57,367
Now I won't be coming back.

24
00:01:57,826 --> 00:01:59,786
Since you're here,
how about a game with me?

25
00:02:01,538 --> 00:02:05,041
If you win, I'll give you
a lifetime membership for free.

26
00:02:05,042 --> 00:02:06,542
But if I win,

27
00:02:06,543 --> 00:02:08,879
you just need to answer my questions.

28
00:02:13,216 --> 00:02:16,135
- Ever heard the word "whippersnapper"?
- No.

29
00:02:16,136 --> 00:02:18,095
I've never heard such a dated word before.

30
00:02:18,096 --> 00:02:21,141
[scoffs] That's what you are.
Look it up when you get home.

31
00:02:21,850 --> 00:02:24,394
Hey, I guess you don't feel confident.

32
00:02:26,688 --> 00:02:28,856
I heard you were
all washed up and retired.

33
00:02:28,857 --> 00:02:30,483
How dare you, you asshole.

34
00:02:30,484 --> 00:02:33,444
I'm talking with your boss here.

35
00:02:33,445 --> 00:02:34,737
Stay out of this, lackey.

36
00:02:34,738 --> 00:02:35,781
[♪ music swells]

37
00:02:37,324 --> 00:02:38,492
Not feeling confident?

38
00:02:39,326 --> 00:02:41,286
About winning against a whippersnapper?

39
00:02:43,038 --> 00:02:44,330
[♪ music fades]

40
00:02:44,331 --> 00:02:45,457
[Seongwook sighs]

41
00:02:46,625 --> 00:02:47,959
The club's management rights.

42
00:02:49,002 --> 00:02:51,379
If you want to bet with me,
make it worth my while.

43
00:02:51,380 --> 00:02:54,090
Whoa, you sure drive a hard bargain.

44
00:02:54,091 --> 00:02:55,174
Deal!

45
00:02:55,175 --> 00:02:57,426
[♪ jaunty, dramatic music playing]

46
00:02:57,427 --> 00:02:58,887
I'll shoot first.

47
00:03:06,687 --> 00:03:07,729
Pull.

48
00:03:08,146 --> 00:03:09,563
[gunshot]

49
00:03:09,564 --> 00:03:10,565
Pull.

50
00:03:11,191 --> 00:03:12,442
- [gunshot]
- [target shatters]

51
00:03:15,112 --> 00:03:16,154
[casings clatter]

52
00:03:21,493 --> 00:03:22,952
Pull.

53
00:03:22,953 --> 00:03:24,037
[gunshot]

54
00:03:24,621 --> 00:03:26,122
Pull.

55
00:03:26,123 --> 00:03:27,165
[gunshot]

56
00:03:27,541 --> 00:03:29,417
So your eyes are still holding up.

57
00:03:29,418 --> 00:03:30,543
What?

58
00:03:30,544 --> 00:03:31,545
[gun clicks]

59
00:03:33,839 --> 00:03:34,840
[Isoo] Pull.

60
00:03:35,382 --> 00:03:36,632
[gunshot]

61
00:03:36,633 --> 00:03:38,009
Pull.

62
00:03:44,307 --> 00:03:45,308
[Seongwook] Pull.

63
00:03:48,645 --> 00:03:49,729
Pull.

64
00:03:50,439 --> 00:03:51,481
[gunshot]

65
00:03:52,732 --> 00:03:54,025
[Isoo] Pull.

66
00:03:55,652 --> 00:03:56,820
Pull.

67
00:03:57,696 --> 00:03:58,738
[gunshot]

68
00:03:59,698 --> 00:04:00,699
[casing clatters]

69
00:04:02,200 --> 00:04:03,701
[Seongwook] Pull.

70
00:04:03,702 --> 00:04:04,703
[gunshot]

71
00:04:05,162 --> 00:04:06,454
Pull.

72
00:04:06,455 --> 00:04:07,622
[target whizzing]

73
00:04:12,669 --> 00:04:13,753
[exhales sharply]

74
00:04:14,379 --> 00:04:16,047
Looks like I won. Huh?

75
00:04:17,549 --> 00:04:19,301
Age catches up with everyone.

76
00:04:21,761 --> 00:04:22,763
[♪ music fades]

77
00:04:32,647 --> 00:04:33,731
EPISODE 8

78
00:04:33,732 --> 00:04:35,775
- [Isoo] Detective Joo.
- What happened?

79
00:04:35,776 --> 00:04:38,110
- What's with the outfit?
- Never mind that.

80
00:04:38,111 --> 00:04:40,237
Ham Seongwook says
he'll tell us everything.

81
00:04:40,238 --> 00:04:41,322
What? How?

82
00:04:41,323 --> 00:04:42,823
- [♪ jaunty music playing]
- [exhales smugly]

83
00:04:42,824 --> 00:04:44,867
I made a bet with him over this club.

84
00:04:44,868 --> 00:04:47,828
People like him can't resist a challenge.

85
00:04:47,829 --> 00:04:49,121
You know it, too.

86
00:04:49,122 --> 00:04:51,332
You made a bet with him over this club?

87
00:04:51,333 --> 00:04:53,168
- Is this yours?
- I bought it yesterday.

88
00:04:53,752 --> 00:04:56,545
The owner was deep in debt,
so he wanted to sell it quickly.

89
00:04:56,546 --> 00:04:58,923
[exhales incredulously] How much was it?

90
00:04:58,924 --> 00:05:01,175
Actually, never mind.
Why would I need to know?

91
00:05:01,176 --> 00:05:04,428
[sighs] I almost missed one shot,
so that really had me sweating.

92
00:05:04,429 --> 00:05:05,805
Because you'd lose the club?

93
00:05:05,806 --> 00:05:07,807
No, because I would lose to him.

94
00:05:07,808 --> 00:05:10,810
How could I live with myself
after losing to a washed-up thug?

95
00:05:10,811 --> 00:05:13,562
That's true.
You can't lose to a washed-up thug.

96
00:05:13,563 --> 00:05:16,398
Anyway, I got him to the table.
I did pretty well, right?

97
00:05:16,399 --> 00:05:19,777
[chuckles] Yes, you did well.
You really are a cheat code.

98
00:05:19,778 --> 00:05:22,029
[clicks tongue, sighs contentedly]

99
00:05:22,030 --> 00:05:23,156
[♪ music fades]

100
00:05:26,201 --> 00:05:28,119
I'm Joo Hyera from Gangha Police.

101
00:05:29,788 --> 00:05:30,871
[Isoo] She's my team leader.

102
00:05:30,872 --> 00:05:32,624
She'll be joining us. Have a seat.

103
00:05:34,501 --> 00:05:35,669
[exhales deeply]

104
00:05:38,880 --> 00:05:41,298
I lost, so I will keep my word.

105
00:05:41,299 --> 00:05:44,051
Oh, like a real man.

106
00:05:44,052 --> 00:05:45,302
Don't lie to us now.

107
00:05:45,303 --> 00:05:47,222
I never lie.

108
00:05:48,056 --> 00:05:51,560
On April 12th, Magician Park Jaeha
died during a performance.

109
00:05:52,352 --> 00:05:54,187
We believe he was murdered.

110
00:05:55,355 --> 00:05:58,692
Please tell us everything that happened
between you and Mr. Park Jaeha.

111
00:06:02,237 --> 00:06:03,613
[♪ soft, suspenseful music playing]

112
00:06:04,531 --> 00:06:07,576
There's an expression
about being the apple of one's eye.

113
00:06:09,244 --> 00:06:10,787
Only someone who's had a child

114
00:06:11,496 --> 00:06:13,206
can understand what that feels like.

115
00:06:15,250 --> 00:06:16,543
My daughter

116
00:06:17,419 --> 00:06:18,628
is the apple of my eye.

117
00:06:20,422 --> 00:06:22,256
When she was little,

118
00:06:22,257 --> 00:06:24,843
my wife died from an illness.

119
00:06:26,678 --> 00:06:27,846
I cherished her,

120
00:06:28,513 --> 00:06:29,806
treasured her,

121
00:06:30,807 --> 00:06:32,642
and raised her with the utmost care.

122
00:06:36,062 --> 00:06:37,730
But not long ago,

123
00:06:37,731 --> 00:06:39,774
she said she got a boyfriend.

124
00:06:40,817 --> 00:06:42,319
So I put my boys on him

125
00:06:43,653 --> 00:06:45,405
to find out what kind of guy he was.

126
00:06:47,115 --> 00:06:48,950
[♪ music turns ominous]

127
00:06:52,621 --> 00:06:53,622
But it turns out...

128
00:07:08,428 --> 00:07:09,637
Seven women?

129
00:07:09,638 --> 00:07:11,639
[inhales sharply, exhales]

130
00:07:11,640 --> 00:07:12,723
Yes.

131
00:07:12,724 --> 00:07:13,932
[scoffs]

132
00:07:13,933 --> 00:07:17,561
And my Sujeong is...
[in English] "Honey 7"?

133
00:07:17,562 --> 00:07:18,813
[♪ music swells]

134
00:07:26,154 --> 00:07:27,363
[♪ music fades]

135
00:07:27,364 --> 00:07:28,782
[in Korean] Bring that bastard to me.

136
00:07:29,658 --> 00:07:30,991
PARK JAEHA'S MAGIC FIRE

137
00:07:30,992 --> 00:07:32,410
[whistling]

138
00:07:33,161 --> 00:07:36,288
[in English] "Park Jaeha's Magic Fire."

139
00:07:36,289 --> 00:07:37,498
- [chuckles smugly]
- [henchman whistles]

140
00:07:37,499 --> 00:07:38,624
[whistles]

141
00:07:38,625 --> 00:07:40,210
[♪ gripping, foreboding music playing]

142
00:07:41,878 --> 00:07:43,212
Park Jaeha?

143
00:07:43,213 --> 00:07:44,546
Yes?

144
00:07:44,547 --> 00:07:45,923
Come with us.

145
00:07:45,924 --> 00:07:47,091
Who are you?

146
00:07:47,092 --> 00:07:48,259
Wait, what is this about?

147
00:07:48,635 --> 00:07:50,302
[exclaims, groans]

148
00:07:50,303 --> 00:07:52,513
- Hey, magician.
- Yes?

149
00:07:52,514 --> 00:07:54,807
Do you want us to beat you up
and drag you away,

150
00:07:54,808 --> 00:07:56,058
or will you come quietly?

151
00:07:56,059 --> 00:07:57,476
[breath trembling]

152
00:07:57,477 --> 00:07:58,895
- I'll come quietly.
- Let's go.

153
00:07:59,312 --> 00:08:00,480
[exclaims in pain]

154
00:08:02,774 --> 00:08:04,650
[♪ music swells, stops]

155
00:08:04,651 --> 00:08:06,110
Seriously, what's this about?

156
00:08:06,111 --> 00:08:10,406
Just try saying one more word.

157
00:08:10,407 --> 00:08:12,282
You'll definitely regret it.

158
00:08:12,283 --> 00:08:14,535
I think you've misunderstood something--
[exclaims]

159
00:08:14,536 --> 00:08:16,287
[♪ tense, foreboding music playing]

160
00:08:18,540 --> 00:08:19,541
Drive.

161
00:08:20,125 --> 00:08:22,000
[tires screeching]

162
00:08:22,001 --> 00:08:23,211
[♪ music swells]

163
00:08:24,838 --> 00:08:25,921
[gasps]

164
00:08:25,922 --> 00:08:26,923
[♪ music fades]

165
00:08:27,590 --> 00:08:29,217
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

166
00:08:30,844 --> 00:08:31,845
[gasps]

167
00:08:33,096 --> 00:08:34,806
I'm Sujeong's father.

168
00:08:40,645 --> 00:08:42,062
I'm sorry.

169
00:08:42,063 --> 00:08:43,772
Please forgive me just once.

170
00:08:43,773 --> 00:08:44,774
Forgive you for what?

171
00:08:46,985 --> 00:08:50,155
I'll break up with her right away,
and I won't ever see her again!

172
00:08:51,156 --> 00:08:52,198
Which means

173
00:08:53,283 --> 00:08:55,869
you never really loved her to begin with?

174
00:08:57,078 --> 00:08:58,162
What?

175
00:08:58,163 --> 00:09:00,873
You never cared about her,
but you dragged my daughter

176
00:09:00,874 --> 00:09:02,208
in and out of hotels?

177
00:09:03,668 --> 00:09:04,711
[exclaims]

178
00:09:05,545 --> 00:09:08,339
I didn't do anything to her.
We only slept holding hands!

179
00:09:09,841 --> 00:09:11,383
It's true!

180
00:09:11,384 --> 00:09:13,094
I swear on my dead mother!

181
00:09:13,803 --> 00:09:15,764
I promise! It's true!

182
00:09:17,849 --> 00:09:19,684
[♪ music increases in tempo]

183
00:09:23,188 --> 00:09:24,314
Which hand?

184
00:09:25,065 --> 00:09:26,357
We promise with the right.

185
00:09:29,694 --> 00:09:30,695
[yelps]

186
00:09:31,279 --> 00:09:32,821
Wait!

187
00:09:32,822 --> 00:09:35,074
What are you doing to me?

188
00:09:35,075 --> 00:09:36,825
I used to be in the mob.

189
00:09:36,826 --> 00:09:38,035
What?

190
00:09:38,036 --> 00:09:40,371
Our mob always pays people back in kind.

191
00:09:41,247 --> 00:09:43,499
Your hand touched my daughter,

192
00:09:43,500 --> 00:09:44,834
so I'm going to take it.

193
00:09:45,585 --> 00:09:47,419
No, you can't!

194
00:09:47,420 --> 00:09:48,921
Don't do this to me!

195
00:09:48,922 --> 00:09:50,005
Just beat me...

196
00:09:50,006 --> 00:09:51,299
[grunts, groans]

197
00:09:52,008 --> 00:09:53,801
Damn it, you hit me again.

198
00:09:53,802 --> 00:09:56,720
Wait, hold on! Please, sir, wait!

199
00:09:56,721 --> 00:09:57,806
Wait.

200
00:09:59,808 --> 00:10:00,809
If I...

201
00:10:01,726 --> 00:10:03,520
lose this hand,

202
00:10:04,479 --> 00:10:05,896
Sujeong will be sad.

203
00:10:05,897 --> 00:10:07,064
- Cut it off.
- [Jaeha] No!

204
00:10:07,065 --> 00:10:08,899
Wait, hold on!

205
00:10:08,900 --> 00:10:11,860
Please wait, sir. Please.

206
00:10:11,861 --> 00:10:13,112
Wait.

207
00:10:13,113 --> 00:10:14,531
[breathing heavily]

208
00:10:15,323 --> 00:10:16,825
Please just let me...

209
00:10:17,951 --> 00:10:19,327
do my last show. [sobbing]

210
00:10:21,371 --> 00:10:23,164
This will be the end

211
00:10:24,290 --> 00:10:26,626
of my life as a magician.

212
00:10:29,003 --> 00:10:30,505
[continues sobbing]

213
00:10:33,758 --> 00:10:36,051
No, sir, please.

214
00:10:36,052 --> 00:10:38,095
- [♪ music fades]
- That's all.

215
00:10:38,096 --> 00:10:40,097
My boys were just waiting there

216
00:10:40,098 --> 00:10:42,058
to bring him to me after the show.

217
00:10:43,726 --> 00:10:45,435
Would his fingers have been enough?

218
00:10:45,436 --> 00:10:48,021
She's your cherished, treasured daughter.

219
00:10:48,022 --> 00:10:49,356
[clicks tongue, inhales deeply]

220
00:10:49,357 --> 00:10:50,440
[exhales] Hey...

221
00:10:50,441 --> 00:10:52,860
I wasn't serious
about cutting his hand off.

222
00:10:52,861 --> 00:10:54,820
I was just... [scoffs softly]

223
00:10:54,821 --> 00:10:56,948
...threatening him
so he'd end things for good.

224
00:10:58,199 --> 00:11:00,827
That bastard was truly
nothing but a spineless coward.

225
00:11:02,912 --> 00:11:03,997
I'm done talking now.

226
00:11:05,582 --> 00:11:06,665
I'll be on my way.

227
00:11:06,666 --> 00:11:07,917
[Sujeong] Dad.

228
00:11:11,963 --> 00:11:13,590
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

229
00:11:14,382 --> 00:11:15,465
Oh, goodness.

230
00:11:15,466 --> 00:11:17,968
My princess. This must've been heavy.

231
00:11:17,969 --> 00:11:20,138
You said you were arriving late.
Hey, take this.

232
00:11:25,143 --> 00:11:26,144
What's wrong?

233
00:11:27,854 --> 00:11:28,938
Was it you?

234
00:11:29,647 --> 00:11:30,648
What do you mean?

235
00:11:31,357 --> 00:11:32,567
[breath trembles]

236
00:11:36,070 --> 00:11:37,113
Hey.

237
00:11:38,448 --> 00:11:39,490
[whispering] It's not loaded.

238
00:11:40,992 --> 00:11:42,075
[sighs softly in relief]

239
00:11:42,076 --> 00:11:43,745
Did you kill him?

240
00:11:44,829 --> 00:11:45,830
I didn't.

241
00:11:46,456 --> 00:11:48,374
[voice shaking] I told you I loved him.

242
00:11:49,542 --> 00:11:51,002
Were you the one who killed him?

243
00:11:58,009 --> 00:11:59,594
[breath trembling]

244
00:12:02,096 --> 00:12:04,349
If you really think I killed him,

245
00:12:05,058 --> 00:12:06,059
pull the trigger.

246
00:12:18,905 --> 00:12:20,240
[♪ music swells]

247
00:12:28,248 --> 00:12:29,332
[♪ music fades]

248
00:12:34,337 --> 00:12:35,755
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

249
00:12:38,925 --> 00:12:42,345
I'll tell you everything
about the kind of man Park Jaeha was.

250
00:12:52,605 --> 00:12:53,939
[♪ music fades]

251
00:12:53,940 --> 00:12:55,358
Can we believe him?

252
00:12:56,067 --> 00:12:57,652
He said he never lies.

253
00:13:00,655 --> 00:13:03,574
Why would he mention
that he threatened to cut off his fingers?

254
00:13:04,158 --> 00:13:06,285
He's confident because he didn't kill him.

255
00:13:06,286 --> 00:13:08,913
Or the victim's dead,
so it doesn't matter if he tells us.

256
00:13:09,706 --> 00:13:13,583
Besides, you have to mix in
a bit of truth when telling a lie.

257
00:13:13,584 --> 00:13:16,546
So you think Ham Seongwook is the culprit?

258
00:13:17,797 --> 00:13:19,007
[sighs thoughtfully]

259
00:13:19,716 --> 00:13:20,717
No.

260
00:13:21,676 --> 00:13:24,094
Ham Seongwook would've killed him quietly.

261
00:13:24,095 --> 00:13:25,929
He'd never do it onstage.

262
00:13:25,930 --> 00:13:27,014
That's true.

263
00:13:27,015 --> 00:13:28,265
[♪ soft, suspenseful music playing]

264
00:13:28,266 --> 00:13:32,145
[inhales sharply] The culprit killed him
while countless people were watching.

265
00:13:33,354 --> 00:13:34,689
That's the crux of this case.

266
00:13:36,941 --> 00:13:37,984
[♪ music fades]

267
00:13:43,489 --> 00:13:44,781
Excuse me.

268
00:13:44,782 --> 00:13:46,826
Oh. Yes, can I help you?

269
00:13:47,744 --> 00:13:49,286
I'm with the police.

270
00:13:49,287 --> 00:13:50,788
Oh, right.

271
00:13:53,916 --> 00:13:57,336
This is you in this photo, isn't it?

272
00:13:58,087 --> 00:13:59,839
Uh, yes, it's me.

273
00:14:00,548 --> 00:14:03,300
Did you notice anything strange
on the day of the incident?

274
00:14:03,301 --> 00:14:05,218
[scoffs softly] Anything strange?

275
00:14:05,219 --> 00:14:06,929
Yes, anything out of the ordinary.

276
00:14:07,847 --> 00:14:09,015
Uh...

277
00:14:10,058 --> 00:14:13,061
[sharp inhale]
That day, I was quite worn out.

278
00:14:13,936 --> 00:14:15,062
I don't know why.

279
00:14:15,063 --> 00:14:18,482
I thought maybe it was because
I had a drink the night before,

280
00:14:18,483 --> 00:14:21,234
but the equipment felt heavy.

281
00:14:21,235 --> 00:14:22,319
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

282
00:14:22,320 --> 00:14:23,821
- Heavy?
- Yes.

283
00:14:26,491 --> 00:14:29,535
Did you see Mr. Park Jaehyung
at the workshop that day?

284
00:14:30,870 --> 00:14:32,537
No, I didn't.

285
00:14:32,538 --> 00:14:34,664
He usually comes out
to check the equipment,

286
00:14:34,665 --> 00:14:36,542
but he wasn't there that day.

287
00:14:37,752 --> 00:14:39,462
- Okay, thank you.
- Sure.

288
00:14:53,768 --> 00:14:55,937
[♪ suspenseful, foreboding music playing]

289
00:15:11,828 --> 00:15:12,954
[sighs softly]

290
00:15:17,917 --> 00:15:19,335
[♪ music increases in tempo]

291
00:15:32,807 --> 00:15:34,183
[♪ music resumes tempo]

292
00:15:35,810 --> 00:15:39,646
ORAL MEDICATION
PARK JAEHYUNG

293
00:15:39,647 --> 00:15:41,606
[♪ suspenseful, ticking music playing]

294
00:15:41,607 --> 00:15:42,692
[pen clicks]

295
00:15:46,988 --> 00:15:48,113
[pen clicks]

296
00:15:48,114 --> 00:15:49,448
[♪ music swells]

297
00:15:50,783 --> 00:15:51,950
[♪ music fades]

298
00:15:51,951 --> 00:15:52,952
[sniffs]

299
00:15:53,327 --> 00:15:54,328
[sniffs]

300
00:15:57,707 --> 00:15:59,500
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

301
00:16:07,592 --> 00:16:09,093
- [jerry can thuds]
- [kerosene sloshing]

302
00:16:20,938 --> 00:16:22,190
- Hello.
- Hello.

303
00:16:23,482 --> 00:16:25,901
I'm Detective Choi Kyungjin
from Gangha Police.

304
00:16:25,902 --> 00:16:27,319
Ah, right.

305
00:16:27,320 --> 00:16:29,863
Did anyone buy kerosene
from here recently?

306
00:16:29,864 --> 00:16:31,865
I think there were a few.

307
00:16:31,866 --> 00:16:33,575
Could you check for me?

308
00:16:33,576 --> 00:16:34,869
Of course.

309
00:16:36,245 --> 00:16:37,413
[exhales softly]

310
00:16:38,581 --> 00:16:40,416
[♪ music increases in tempo]

311
00:16:45,171 --> 00:16:46,589
[♪ music swells]

312
00:16:48,507 --> 00:16:50,259
- [chuckles softly]
- [♪ music fades]

313
00:16:52,929 --> 00:16:54,222
[Isoo] Mmm...

314
00:16:54,805 --> 00:16:57,766
If Ham Seongwook isn't the killer...

315
00:16:57,767 --> 00:16:59,769
Let's think this through
from the beginning. [sighs]

316
00:17:01,229 --> 00:17:05,398
The three women
who have access to the equipment.

317
00:17:05,399 --> 00:17:06,733
And also,

318
00:17:06,734 --> 00:17:08,361
Park Jaehyung.

319
00:17:10,863 --> 00:17:12,364
[Isoo sighs thoughtfully]

320
00:17:12,365 --> 00:17:13,491
[Hyera sighs softly]

321
00:17:16,702 --> 00:17:17,827
Where were you?

322
00:17:17,828 --> 00:17:18,955
[sighs wearily]

323
00:17:19,538 --> 00:17:21,331
I went to the theater.

324
00:17:21,332 --> 00:17:23,500
Park Jaehyung wasn't
in the workshop that day.

325
00:17:23,501 --> 00:17:24,502
Huh?

326
00:17:25,336 --> 00:17:26,379
Then what happened?

327
00:17:27,338 --> 00:17:28,755
He was there when we went.

328
00:17:28,756 --> 00:17:30,466
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

329
00:17:33,719 --> 00:17:35,263
Mr. Park Jaeha?

330
00:17:38,099 --> 00:17:39,392
I'm Park Jaehyung.

331
00:17:40,184 --> 00:17:41,393
Jaeha's brother.

332
00:17:41,394 --> 00:17:42,894
The staff didn't see him.

333
00:17:42,895 --> 00:17:46,064
And there was a heater in the workshop.

334
00:17:46,065 --> 00:17:47,190
A kerosene heater.

335
00:17:47,191 --> 00:17:48,651
The kerosene can was half empty.

336
00:17:52,989 --> 00:17:55,199
I found out who bought the kerosene.

337
00:17:57,785 --> 00:18:00,078
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

338
00:18:00,079 --> 00:18:02,957
No one bought kerosene
from gas stations near the theater,

339
00:18:03,624 --> 00:18:05,792
so I checked the suspects' neighborhoods.

340
00:18:05,793 --> 00:18:06,877
[keyboard key clacks]

341
00:18:31,819 --> 00:18:32,945
[keyboard key clacks]

342
00:18:33,738 --> 00:18:34,988
That's Ms. Lee Jiyun.

343
00:18:34,989 --> 00:18:37,283
I told you! I was right.

344
00:18:38,159 --> 00:18:41,786
Lee Jiyun and Park Jaehyung
were working together.

345
00:18:41,787 --> 00:18:45,040
[sighs smugly]
God, my instincts are unbelievable.

346
00:18:45,041 --> 00:18:46,292
He might be right.

347
00:18:47,543 --> 00:18:51,463
I found medication in his workshop.
I checked with the hospital.

348
00:18:51,464 --> 00:18:53,048
He has terminal cancer.

349
00:18:53,049 --> 00:18:54,091
No way.

350
00:18:54,634 --> 00:18:55,676
[sighs softly]

351
00:18:59,430 --> 00:19:01,556
On the verge of death,

352
00:19:01,557 --> 00:19:03,976
he wanted to kill his brother,
whom he was jealous of?

353
00:19:04,560 --> 00:19:06,061
[sighs deeply]

354
00:19:06,062 --> 00:19:08,146
He must've felt so wronged, huh?

355
00:19:08,147 --> 00:19:11,149
He's going to die anyway,
so why not take his brother with him?

356
00:19:11,150 --> 00:19:13,944
And Ms. Lee Jiyun joined his plan
after being betrayed.

357
00:19:20,576 --> 00:19:23,454
[Hyera] <i>Park Jaehyung poured kerosene
into the equipment.</i>

358
00:19:28,793 --> 00:19:29,877
[in English] Okay.

359
00:19:31,462 --> 00:19:33,881
[Hyera, in Korean] <i>And Lee Jiyun
pretended not to know?</i>

360
00:19:34,590 --> 00:19:36,007
Find out where Lee Jiyun is.

361
00:19:36,008 --> 00:19:37,093
Got it.

362
00:19:45,142 --> 00:19:46,267
[♪ music fades]

363
00:19:46,268 --> 00:19:47,395
DIRECTOR LEE JIYUN

364
00:20:02,243 --> 00:20:03,285
- [sighs]
- [box snaps shut]

365
00:20:05,037 --> 00:20:06,038
[knock at door]

366
00:20:10,793 --> 00:20:12,752
- [Hyera] Ms. Lee Jiyun.
- Yes?

367
00:20:12,753 --> 00:20:15,171
- [door closes]
- [Hyera] Can we have a word with you?

368
00:20:15,172 --> 00:20:16,841
- Sure.
- [Isoo] Oh...

369
00:20:17,425 --> 00:20:19,593
- It looks like you were packing.
- [Jiyun, softly] Mmm.

370
00:20:20,386 --> 00:20:22,138
The show's over now.

371
00:20:23,180 --> 00:20:24,639
I need to find another project.

372
00:20:24,640 --> 00:20:25,641
[Isoo] Mmm...

373
00:20:26,600 --> 00:20:27,852
So, what can I do for you?

374
00:20:28,686 --> 00:20:31,354
Two days before the incident,
at Sankyeong Gas Station,

375
00:20:31,355 --> 00:20:32,815
you bought kerosene, didn't you?

376
00:20:34,859 --> 00:20:35,942
Yes, I did.

377
00:20:35,943 --> 00:20:36,944
Why?

378
00:20:37,737 --> 00:20:39,572
- To kill the one who betrayed you?
- What?

379
00:20:40,156 --> 00:20:41,239
[Isoo inhales sharply]

380
00:20:41,240 --> 00:20:44,534
You gave your boyfriend of one year
money to get a place together,

381
00:20:44,535 --> 00:20:47,579
only to find he had seven girlfriends.
You must've been furious.

382
00:20:47,580 --> 00:20:49,206
I understand. Mmm.

383
00:20:49,915 --> 00:20:51,959
What are you talking about?

384
00:20:53,043 --> 00:20:55,462
We found kerosene inside the casket.

385
00:20:55,463 --> 00:20:56,588
[♪ tense music playing]

386
00:20:56,589 --> 00:20:59,424
You're the only one
who bought kerosene before the incident.

387
00:20:59,425 --> 00:21:01,635
Jaehyung asked me to buy it for him.

388
00:21:02,636 --> 00:21:04,680
The workshop gets cold,
so he uses a heater.

389
00:21:05,639 --> 00:21:07,640
He can't go out in a wheelchair to buy it.

390
00:21:07,641 --> 00:21:09,017
Mmm...

391
00:21:09,018 --> 00:21:12,062
Is that all you did for him?
I have a feeling you did more.

392
00:21:12,813 --> 00:21:16,316
Why are you doing this to me?
I'm already pissed off as it is.

393
00:21:16,317 --> 00:21:19,153
You knew he was going to kill
his brother, didn't you?

394
00:21:20,196 --> 00:21:21,905
You knew and looked the other way.

395
00:21:21,906 --> 00:21:22,907
Or...

396
00:21:23,699 --> 00:21:25,242
were you in on it from the start?

397
00:21:25,868 --> 00:21:27,328
[Jiyun] Detective.

398
00:21:27,953 --> 00:21:30,122
I'm not that dumb.

399
00:21:31,457 --> 00:21:32,791
Of course, I'm angry.

400
00:21:32,792 --> 00:21:34,585
It wasn't just another woman or two.

401
00:21:35,211 --> 00:21:37,254
But I didn't know that
until after he died.

402
00:21:38,047 --> 00:21:39,882
Even if I had known,

403
00:21:40,758 --> 00:21:43,219
why would I ruin my life
over a bastard like that?

404
00:21:44,178 --> 00:21:45,553
I'd get caught this quickly.

405
00:21:45,554 --> 00:21:47,515
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

406
00:21:50,142 --> 00:21:53,854
If you're still that suspicious,
I'll do a polygraph, or whatever it takes.

407
00:21:55,856 --> 00:21:57,149
I'll do it all!

408
00:21:58,943 --> 00:21:59,985
[♪ music swells]

409
00:22:02,780 --> 00:22:03,905
[♪ music fades]

410
00:22:03,906 --> 00:22:06,450
NATIONAL FORENSIC SERVICE

411
00:22:09,036 --> 00:22:10,830
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

412
00:22:12,540 --> 00:22:13,791
[camera shutter clicking]

413
00:22:20,381 --> 00:22:22,049
[Dr. Yoon] I'll begin the autopsy.

414
00:22:33,143 --> 00:22:34,603
[♪ music increases in tempo]

415
00:22:52,913 --> 00:22:53,914
[grunts softly]

416
00:22:57,668 --> 00:22:58,919
[♪ music resumes tempo]

417
00:22:59,712 --> 00:23:02,423
The older one had cancer,
the other was hunted by thugs.

418
00:23:04,258 --> 00:23:05,259
Uh...

419
00:23:06,302 --> 00:23:07,595
But why didn't he run away?

420
00:23:08,345 --> 00:23:09,762
[Hyera] What?

421
00:23:09,763 --> 00:23:12,390
Ham Seongwook was going to cut off
his fingers that day.

422
00:23:12,391 --> 00:23:14,143
Why didn't he run away?

423
00:23:19,815 --> 00:23:20,816
[sniffs]

424
00:23:21,400 --> 00:23:23,318
[gasps softly] Detective Park.

425
00:23:23,319 --> 00:23:24,695
[♪ music increases in tempo]

426
00:23:35,497 --> 00:23:37,374
[♪ music swells, fades]

427
00:23:38,292 --> 00:23:39,375
[Isoo sighs softly]

428
00:23:39,376 --> 00:23:40,628
[cell phone vibrating]

429
00:23:43,172 --> 00:23:44,255
Hello, Dr. Yoon.

430
00:23:44,256 --> 00:23:46,258
The victim didn't burn to death.

431
00:23:46,842 --> 00:23:49,677
There's no soot in his trachea or bronchi.

432
00:23:49,678 --> 00:23:50,762
Then...

433
00:23:50,763 --> 00:23:52,138
[♪ tense, ticking music playing]

434
00:23:52,139 --> 00:23:55,726
He was already dead before the fire.

435
00:23:58,228 --> 00:24:00,105
- [line disconnects]
- What is it?

436
00:24:01,857 --> 00:24:03,817
He was already dead before the fire.

437
00:24:06,320 --> 00:24:07,321
[Kyungjin] Detective Joo!

438
00:24:08,155 --> 00:24:10,198
[♪ upbeat rock music playing]

439
00:24:10,199 --> 00:24:11,866
[panting] It's the same size
as the casket.

440
00:24:11,867 --> 00:24:13,243
And it smells of kerosene.

441
00:24:17,623 --> 00:24:19,332
It wasn't Park Jaeha.

442
00:24:19,333 --> 00:24:21,042
Park Jaehyung is the one who died.

443
00:24:21,043 --> 00:24:22,336
[scoffs incredulously]

444
00:24:25,923 --> 00:24:28,049
The one who had to disappear
was Park Jaeha.

445
00:24:28,050 --> 00:24:30,177
So he vanishes in the middle of his act?

446
00:24:31,512 --> 00:24:33,931
He kills Park Jaehyung
and puts him inside the casket.

447
00:24:34,598 --> 00:24:35,599
[thuds]

448
00:24:40,396 --> 00:24:42,022
[Isoo] <i>Then he disappears
during the show...</i>

449
00:24:43,941 --> 00:24:44,984
[flames whooshing]

450
00:24:47,778 --> 00:24:49,404
Making Park Jaeha the victim.

451
00:24:49,405 --> 00:24:51,364
Because they're twins.

452
00:24:51,365 --> 00:24:52,825
This is basically teleportation.

453
00:24:53,659 --> 00:24:55,035
We just need his fingerprint.

454
00:24:55,619 --> 00:24:56,620
Let's go.

455
00:24:58,580 --> 00:24:59,623
[♪ music fades]

456
00:25:03,585 --> 00:25:04,586
[exhales softly]

457
00:25:08,382 --> 00:25:09,591
Mr. Park Jaeha!

458
00:25:11,677 --> 00:25:12,720
Mr. Park Jaehyung!

459
00:25:14,388 --> 00:25:15,889
There you are.

460
00:25:16,640 --> 00:25:17,724
What were you up to?

461
00:25:17,725 --> 00:25:19,267
I have to clear this place out.

462
00:25:19,268 --> 00:25:22,603
- Oh, that's a lot of work. Let me help.
- No, it's all right.

463
00:25:22,604 --> 00:25:24,230
[♪ dramatic spy music playing]

464
00:25:24,231 --> 00:25:25,857
I'm going to take my time.

465
00:25:25,858 --> 00:25:28,027
[Isoo] You shouldn't push yourself
in your condition.

466
00:25:28,736 --> 00:25:30,612
- Shall I pack this?
- Don't touch...

467
00:25:33,741 --> 00:25:34,824
[in English] Magic.

468
00:25:34,825 --> 00:25:36,242
Magic...

469
00:25:36,243 --> 00:25:39,037
[in Korean] Did it disappear?
How did this...

470
00:25:39,038 --> 00:25:40,538
Jin Isoo.

471
00:25:40,539 --> 00:25:41,999
Stop bothering him and let's go.

472
00:25:42,666 --> 00:25:43,834
Sorry to bother you.

473
00:25:44,793 --> 00:25:45,877
Jeez.

474
00:25:45,878 --> 00:25:48,296
Let us know if you need any help.

475
00:25:48,297 --> 00:25:50,507
Anything, anytime. Detective Jin.

476
00:25:51,717 --> 00:25:52,885
[Jaehyung, softly] Goodness.

477
00:25:59,808 --> 00:26:01,643
[♪ music increases in tempo]

478
00:26:02,269 --> 00:26:03,479
Sir!

479
00:26:04,897 --> 00:26:06,355
We need fingerprints.

480
00:26:06,356 --> 00:26:07,608
[Kyungjin] It's urgent.

481
00:26:08,067 --> 00:26:09,400
[♪ music fades]

482
00:26:09,401 --> 00:26:11,986
[Hyera] He kept up the wheelchair act
even with no one around.

483
00:26:11,987 --> 00:26:14,864
He's very meticulous.

484
00:26:14,865 --> 00:26:16,449
We were really in sync just now.

485
00:26:16,450 --> 00:26:19,410
[chuckles] Yeah,
your acting is pretty good.

486
00:26:19,411 --> 00:26:22,247
[exhales smugly]
I'm just too talented for my own good.

487
00:26:23,332 --> 00:26:26,710
[sighs heavily]
Anyway, I've never seen a case like this.

488
00:26:27,586 --> 00:26:29,713
He killed his own brother to disappear.

489
00:26:30,714 --> 00:26:33,049
Let's get him
the second we get his fingerprints.

490
00:26:33,050 --> 00:26:34,509
I'll be the one to cuff him.

491
00:26:34,510 --> 00:26:36,011
[chuckles softly] Sure.

492
00:26:37,387 --> 00:26:39,348
[♪ gripping, suspenseful music playing]

493
00:26:41,809 --> 00:26:42,893
[tape ripping]

494
00:26:54,738 --> 00:26:56,156
[♪ music increases in tempo]

495
00:27:03,163 --> 00:27:04,247
[♪ music fades]

496
00:27:04,248 --> 00:27:05,582
- [cell phone vibrating]
- [Isoo sighs]

497
00:27:10,838 --> 00:27:12,130
- [Junyoung] <i>Detective Joo.</i>
- Yes?

498
00:27:12,131 --> 00:27:13,715
We didn't find any fingerprints.

499
00:27:14,299 --> 00:27:15,508
Huh?

500
00:27:15,509 --> 00:27:18,387
They say he would've suffered burns
while working with fire.

501
00:27:19,012 --> 00:27:20,972
We'll see if there are any other ways.

502
00:27:20,973 --> 00:27:22,723
Okay, got it.

503
00:27:22,724 --> 00:27:23,975
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

504
00:27:23,976 --> 00:27:25,893
He was packing a passport earlier.

505
00:27:25,894 --> 00:27:27,563
If he bolts, we'll never catch him.

506
00:27:28,272 --> 00:27:29,438
[sighs in exasperation]

507
00:27:29,439 --> 00:27:31,275
We need a clever way to...

508
00:27:31,775 --> 00:27:33,276
[♪ bright musical sting]

509
00:27:33,277 --> 00:27:35,278
There is a clever way.

510
00:27:35,279 --> 00:27:36,988
[♪ jaunty, suspenseful music playing]

511
00:27:36,989 --> 00:27:37,990
Like what?

512
00:27:38,740 --> 00:27:40,492
Stay here and don't let him get away.

513
00:27:42,953 --> 00:27:45,955
I'll make him shout out
that he's Park Jaeha.

514
00:27:45,956 --> 00:27:47,124
Jin Isoo!

515
00:27:49,001 --> 00:27:50,335
- [sighs softly]
- [♪ music fades]

516
00:27:50,961 --> 00:27:52,629
Why did he suddenly call for us?

517
00:27:53,881 --> 00:27:55,464
- You're all here!
- Hello.

518
00:27:55,465 --> 00:27:56,717
What a relief.

519
00:27:57,342 --> 00:27:58,844
- It's been a while.
- Yes, sir.

520
00:27:58,969 --> 00:28:01,470
I have an urgent project.

521
00:28:01,471 --> 00:28:03,681
What's the name
of that movie we're working on?

522
00:28:03,682 --> 00:28:05,933
<i>The End of Humanity.</i>

523
00:28:05,934 --> 00:28:08,603
Let's rehearse Scene 27.

524
00:28:08,604 --> 00:28:09,687
Right now.

525
00:28:09,688 --> 00:28:11,273
[♪ upbeat rock music playing]

526
00:28:18,030 --> 00:28:19,114
[tires screech]

527
00:28:19,656 --> 00:28:21,116
[tires screech]

528
00:28:25,621 --> 00:28:26,747
ISCG INFECTION CONTROL

529
00:28:34,755 --> 00:28:36,298
[♪ upbeat rock music continues]

530
00:28:47,559 --> 00:28:50,978
PROJECT ISCG:
THE END OF HUMANITY

531
00:28:50,979 --> 00:28:52,022
[♪ music fades]

532
00:28:54,650 --> 00:28:55,651
[grunts softly]

533
00:28:56,777 --> 00:28:57,778
[exhales softly]

534
00:28:59,655 --> 00:29:00,656
[sighs deeply]

535
00:29:03,617 --> 00:29:05,452
Time to say goodbye to this place.

536
00:29:06,036 --> 00:29:07,204
[scoffs softly]

537
00:29:09,247 --> 00:29:10,581
[Isoo] Mr. Park Jaehyung.

538
00:29:10,582 --> 00:29:12,875
Mr. Park Jaehyung! Where are you?

539
00:29:12,876 --> 00:29:14,585
Ah! Are you Park Jaehyung?

540
00:29:14,586 --> 00:29:16,504
Yes, I am.

541
00:29:16,505 --> 00:29:18,297
- [♪ quirky, dramatic music playing]
- [sprayers hissing]

542
00:29:18,298 --> 00:29:20,717
[Isoo] Did you have blood tests done
at Munsan Hospital?

543
00:29:21,718 --> 00:29:25,347
A deadly, contagious virus
was found in your blood.

544
00:29:25,764 --> 00:29:26,847
What?

545
00:29:26,848 --> 00:29:29,266
[Isoo] This is a virus
that's never been identified before.

546
00:29:29,267 --> 00:29:30,686
If this gets out...

547
00:29:31,561 --> 00:29:32,896
it's the end of humanity.

548
00:29:33,313 --> 00:29:34,314
What?

549
00:29:35,107 --> 00:29:37,233
[Kyungjin] It looks like
the virus is only in here!

550
00:29:37,234 --> 00:29:38,776
It hasn't spread outside.

551
00:29:38,777 --> 00:29:41,446
[Junyoung] We must kill the host
and burn this whole place down!

552
00:29:41,863 --> 00:29:43,280
[Isoo] Let's take him to the lab.

553
00:29:43,281 --> 00:29:45,408
[Kyungjin] What if more people
get infected?

554
00:29:45,409 --> 00:29:48,035
Tens of thousands could die
before we have a vaccine!

555
00:29:48,036 --> 00:29:49,704
[Junyoung mutters, grunts]

556
00:29:49,705 --> 00:29:51,872
[gasps] Wait, hold on!

557
00:29:51,873 --> 00:29:53,500
[Junyoung] We must kill him here!

558
00:29:54,543 --> 00:29:57,336
[Isoo, sighs] Is this truly the only way?

559
00:29:57,337 --> 00:29:59,423
[Kyungjin] If we keep quiet,
we can stop a catastrophe.

560
00:30:00,424 --> 00:30:02,050
[Junyoung] I'll take responsibility.

561
00:30:04,928 --> 00:30:06,013
[Isoo] Mr. Park Jaehyung.

562
00:30:07,014 --> 00:30:08,015
We're sorry.

563
00:30:09,182 --> 00:30:10,891
Your sacrifice will save humanity.

564
00:30:10,892 --> 00:30:12,184
What?

565
00:30:12,185 --> 00:30:15,062
[Isoo] You are our hero,
Mr. Park Jaehyung.

566
00:30:15,063 --> 00:30:16,231
[Kyungjin, in English] Hero.

567
00:30:19,359 --> 00:30:20,861
[Isoo, in Korean] We promise

568
00:30:21,361 --> 00:30:22,445
to remember you.

569
00:30:22,446 --> 00:30:23,821
Shoot him.

570
00:30:23,822 --> 00:30:26,365
- [Junyoung grunts]
- Wait! Please, wait.

571
00:30:26,366 --> 00:30:27,367
Wait.

572
00:30:29,703 --> 00:30:30,704
I'm...

573
00:30:31,705 --> 00:30:32,997
not Park Jaehyung.

574
00:30:32,998 --> 00:30:35,291
[Isoo] Do not be afraid of death.
Shoot him.

575
00:30:35,292 --> 00:30:36,584
- [Junyoung grunts]
- [Jaehyung] Wait, please!

576
00:30:36,585 --> 00:30:37,752
Wait.

577
00:30:37,753 --> 00:30:38,754
I'm...

578
00:30:39,671 --> 00:30:41,047
not Park Jaehyung.

579
00:30:41,048 --> 00:30:42,506
I'm Park Jaeha, his brother!

580
00:30:42,507 --> 00:30:45,051
[Isoo] Mr. Park Jaeha died a few days ago.

581
00:30:45,052 --> 00:30:46,970
- [Junyoung grunts]
- Wait, stop!

582
00:30:47,679 --> 00:30:48,763
I'm...

583
00:30:48,764 --> 00:30:50,890
I'm the magician, Park Jaeha!

584
00:30:50,891 --> 00:30:52,683
- Look!
- [all exclaim in disbelief]

585
00:30:52,684 --> 00:30:54,769
[Jaeha] Look.

586
00:30:54,770 --> 00:30:57,396
My brother couldn't walk
after his accident, but look.

587
00:30:57,397 --> 00:30:58,939
Park Jaeha's magic fire!

588
00:30:58,940 --> 00:31:01,734
The waltz.

589
00:31:01,735 --> 00:31:02,818
Look. See?

590
00:31:02,819 --> 00:31:04,695
I'm light on my feet! See that?

591
00:31:04,696 --> 00:31:05,863
- Right?
- [Isoo, in English] What the...

592
00:31:05,864 --> 00:31:08,032
[in Korean] I'm Jaeha!

593
00:31:08,033 --> 00:31:09,742
[Isoo, in English] Oh, my God.

594
00:31:09,743 --> 00:31:10,826
[in Korean] Who?

595
00:31:10,827 --> 00:31:13,329
Park Jaeha!

596
00:31:13,330 --> 00:31:14,331
[Kyungjin] Wow.

597
00:31:14,998 --> 00:31:16,415
[Isoo scoffs incredulously]

598
00:31:16,416 --> 00:31:17,541
[in English] Jesus.

599
00:31:17,542 --> 00:31:18,793
[in Korean] Park Jaeha.

600
00:31:18,794 --> 00:31:20,796
Huh? Huh?

601
00:31:21,588 --> 00:31:23,380
You said you're Park Jaeha, right?

602
00:31:23,381 --> 00:31:25,092
[♪ upbeat swing jazz music playing]

603
00:31:25,926 --> 00:31:26,927
Park Jaeha.

604
00:31:27,511 --> 00:31:30,096
You're under arrest
for the murder of Park Jaehyung.

605
00:31:30,097 --> 00:31:31,223
[handcuffs clicking]

606
00:31:34,184 --> 00:31:35,393
[exhales heavily]

607
00:31:36,103 --> 00:31:37,104
[sighs softly]

608
00:31:37,646 --> 00:31:38,772
[exclaims smugly]

609
00:31:39,981 --> 00:31:42,483
You're pretty startled
for a magician, huh?

610
00:31:42,484 --> 00:31:43,651
[in English] Surprise!

611
00:31:43,652 --> 00:31:45,945
That virus...

612
00:31:45,946 --> 00:31:47,238
[in Korean] It's a trick.

613
00:31:47,239 --> 00:31:49,366
A show just for Park Jaeha.

614
00:31:50,200 --> 00:31:51,201
[yelps]

615
00:31:52,077 --> 00:31:53,453
[whimpers, gasps]

616
00:31:59,292 --> 00:32:00,377
[softly] What?

617
00:32:00,836 --> 00:32:01,919
[exhales incredulously]

618
00:32:01,920 --> 00:32:02,921
What on earth?

619
00:32:05,423 --> 00:32:08,175
What's ISCG?
It's not part of the police, is it?

620
00:32:08,176 --> 00:32:09,553
[Isoo] This?

621
00:32:12,764 --> 00:32:15,307
ISOO COOL GUY

622
00:32:15,308 --> 00:32:16,392
[♪ music fades]

623
00:32:16,393 --> 00:32:18,311
SEOUL GANGHA POLICE STATION

624
00:32:20,272 --> 00:32:22,023
Tell us what happened.

625
00:32:23,066 --> 00:32:24,860
Sujeong's dad

626
00:32:25,777 --> 00:32:27,987
sent his men to take me to him.

627
00:32:27,988 --> 00:32:29,114
[Seongwook] Your hand

628
00:32:30,282 --> 00:32:31,490
is mine.

629
00:32:31,491 --> 00:32:32,868
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

630
00:32:36,580 --> 00:32:37,789
Cut it off.

631
00:32:41,209 --> 00:32:42,210
Wait.

632
00:32:44,713 --> 00:32:45,796
Aren't you afraid?

633
00:32:45,797 --> 00:32:47,257
The only thing I'm afraid of...

634
00:32:47,966 --> 00:32:50,010
is not keeping my promise to the audience.

635
00:32:51,428 --> 00:32:52,721
It's a shame. [sighs]

636
00:32:53,597 --> 00:32:56,057
I'd hoped a man like you
would become my son-in-law.

637
00:32:58,185 --> 00:33:00,145
That's not what we heard.

638
00:33:01,438 --> 00:33:02,522
[sighs regretfully]

639
00:33:03,648 --> 00:33:04,983
So I told him.

640
00:33:08,361 --> 00:33:09,988
Once I finish my final performance,

641
00:33:11,156 --> 00:33:13,241
I will come back here on my own. And then,

642
00:33:14,242 --> 00:33:15,452
you can take my hand.

643
00:33:18,121 --> 00:33:19,580
Did you really mean that?

644
00:33:19,581 --> 00:33:22,542
- [♪ music fades]
- No. In all honesty,

645
00:33:24,586 --> 00:33:25,711
I just couldn't do it.

646
00:33:25,712 --> 00:33:28,423
How can a magician live without his hands?
Huh?

647
00:33:29,966 --> 00:33:32,802
I spent all day thinking it over,

648
00:33:35,513 --> 00:33:37,014
then I went to see my brother.

649
00:33:37,015 --> 00:33:38,391
[♪ foreboding music playing]

650
00:33:39,017 --> 00:33:41,311
Because I need money to run away.

651
00:33:45,899 --> 00:33:46,900
Jaehyung.

652
00:33:49,736 --> 00:33:50,737
Jaehyung.

653
00:33:57,160 --> 00:33:58,161
[gasps softly]

654
00:33:58,954 --> 00:33:59,955
Jaehyung.

655
00:34:02,207 --> 00:34:03,625
ORAL MEDICATION

656
00:34:05,001 --> 00:34:06,086
[breath trembles]

657
00:34:08,630 --> 00:34:09,839
<i>But</i>

658
00:34:11,007 --> 00:34:12,424
he was dead.

659
00:34:12,425 --> 00:34:13,884
[♪ music swells, fades]

660
00:34:13,885 --> 00:34:14,928
[Isoo] Hey.

661
00:34:15,762 --> 00:34:17,430
If you lie, we'll know.

662
00:34:18,056 --> 00:34:20,015
[frantically] I'm not lying.
It's the truth.

663
00:34:20,016 --> 00:34:22,685
I promise. I even have his suicide note.

664
00:34:22,686 --> 00:34:24,478
[exhales sharply] I promise.

665
00:34:24,479 --> 00:34:26,272
Anyway... [breath trembling]

666
00:34:26,273 --> 00:34:27,899
...I knew he had cancer,

667
00:34:28,566 --> 00:34:31,277
but I didn't know it was that serious.

668
00:34:31,278 --> 00:34:33,655
It seems there was no way to treat it.

669
00:34:34,406 --> 00:34:35,781
So then what did you do?

670
00:34:35,782 --> 00:34:36,991
At first...

671
00:34:36,992 --> 00:34:38,617
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

672
00:34:38,618 --> 00:34:40,160
...I was really shaken up...

673
00:34:40,161 --> 00:34:41,663
[breathing heavily]

674
00:34:47,043 --> 00:34:49,170
<i>but then I thought,</i>

675
00:34:50,422 --> 00:34:52,382
<i>"I really am lucky."</i>

676
00:34:53,091 --> 00:34:55,134
We're twins,

677
00:34:55,135 --> 00:34:57,470
so it's the perfect way to disappear.
[chuckles]

678
00:34:58,805 --> 00:35:01,765
Oh. So,

679
00:35:01,766 --> 00:35:05,060
your brother died,
but you came up with that perfect plan?

680
00:35:05,061 --> 00:35:06,270
[sighs]

681
00:35:06,271 --> 00:35:07,731
He was already dead,

682
00:35:08,815 --> 00:35:11,442
so I thought he was
helping me until the very end.

683
00:35:11,443 --> 00:35:12,944
[♪ gripping, foreboding music playing]

684
00:35:16,281 --> 00:35:17,740
FAREWELL NOTE

685
00:35:17,741 --> 00:35:19,283
DAILY LIFE WAS PAINFUL

686
00:35:19,284 --> 00:35:21,036
THANK YOU ALL FOR EVERYTHING

687
00:35:29,544 --> 00:35:31,379
[♪ music increases in tempo]

688
00:36:06,873 --> 00:36:08,582
[♪ music slows, fades]

689
00:36:08,583 --> 00:36:09,917
Jaeha.

690
00:36:09,918 --> 00:36:11,086
Hey, Luna.

691
00:36:11,920 --> 00:36:14,464
I had a really scary dream today.

692
00:36:15,215 --> 00:36:16,216
What kind of dream?

693
00:36:17,300 --> 00:36:18,968
A dream about you dying.

694
00:36:19,678 --> 00:36:20,804
Ah.

695
00:36:21,471 --> 00:36:23,555
Can't you skip today's show?

696
00:36:23,556 --> 00:36:25,141
[♪ tense, suspenseful music playing]

697
00:36:27,936 --> 00:36:30,562
I have to treat it
like my last performance

698
00:36:30,563 --> 00:36:32,190
and do my best.

699
00:36:40,448 --> 00:36:41,533
[gunshot]

700
00:36:41,908 --> 00:36:43,118
[♪ music increases in tempo]

701
00:37:06,891 --> 00:37:08,267
[fire roaring]

702
00:37:08,268 --> 00:37:09,893
- [burning wood crashes]
- [Dahee screams]

703
00:37:09,894 --> 00:37:11,603
[screaming in horror]

704
00:37:11,604 --> 00:37:13,106
[audience exclaiming in horror]

705
00:37:14,023 --> 00:37:15,524
Get everyone to safety first.

706
00:37:15,525 --> 00:37:16,901
[clamoring]

707
00:37:23,032 --> 00:37:24,533
[♪ music fades]

708
00:37:24,534 --> 00:37:26,286
[♪ tense, foreboding music playing]

709
00:37:29,581 --> 00:37:30,957
[♪ music increases in tempo]

710
00:37:37,964 --> 00:37:39,591
[breathing heavily]

711
00:37:42,302 --> 00:37:43,635
[knock at door]

712
00:37:43,636 --> 00:37:45,680
[Isoo] Hello? This is the police.

713
00:37:51,895 --> 00:37:53,187
[switch clicks]

714
00:37:53,188 --> 00:37:54,563
[wheelchair whirs]

715
00:37:54,564 --> 00:37:55,690
[♪ music swells]

716
00:37:57,734 --> 00:37:58,859
[♪ music fades]

717
00:37:58,860 --> 00:38:01,153
So you burned your dead brother

718
00:38:01,154 --> 00:38:02,863
to disappear completely?

719
00:38:02,864 --> 00:38:05,825
Of course, I didn't feel good about it.

720
00:38:07,076 --> 00:38:09,244
But he was going to be cremated anyway.

721
00:38:09,245 --> 00:38:10,413
[sighs sarcastically]

722
00:38:12,749 --> 00:38:14,667
[exhales] I'm so touched.

723
00:38:15,585 --> 00:38:18,295
Is this what people call
the total package?

724
00:38:18,296 --> 00:38:20,923
Love life, family, colleagues,
performance, character.

725
00:38:20,924 --> 00:38:22,217
All completely trash.

726
00:38:22,842 --> 00:38:23,926
Trash?

727
00:38:23,927 --> 00:38:26,136
I've never met anyone so obnoxious before.

728
00:38:26,137 --> 00:38:27,387
[breathing heavily]

729
00:38:27,388 --> 00:38:29,097
[♪ quirky, dramatic music playing]

730
00:38:29,098 --> 00:38:30,224
What else could I do?

731
00:38:30,225 --> 00:38:31,475
I was scared.

732
00:38:31,476 --> 00:38:33,477
Ever had your hand go into a straw cutter?

733
00:38:33,478 --> 00:38:34,938
It's really sharp.

734
00:38:36,189 --> 00:38:38,774
Anyway, all I did

735
00:38:38,775 --> 00:38:40,944
was burn my brother's dead body,

736
00:38:41,736 --> 00:38:44,948
so is there any chance
I could get a suspended sentence?

737
00:38:46,908 --> 00:38:47,909
Isoo Cool Guy.

738
00:38:49,118 --> 00:38:50,203
Uncross your fingers.

739
00:38:51,579 --> 00:38:53,498
Suspended sentence, my ass.

740
00:38:54,415 --> 00:38:57,042
You think the judges are
crazy enough to do that, huh?

741
00:38:57,043 --> 00:38:58,378
What's the matter with you?

742
00:38:59,546 --> 00:39:00,963
Aren't you being a bit harsh?

743
00:39:00,964 --> 00:39:02,589
- Come here.
- [exclaims]

744
00:39:02,590 --> 00:39:03,674
[♪ music fades]

745
00:39:03,675 --> 00:39:05,050
Jaeha's alive?

746
00:39:05,051 --> 00:39:06,760
Yes. Uh...

747
00:39:06,761 --> 00:39:09,179
He used his dead brother
so he could run away.

748
00:39:09,180 --> 00:39:11,057
Huh? That's so creepy.

749
00:39:11,683 --> 00:39:13,475
Then the dream I had...

750
00:39:13,476 --> 00:39:15,853
Mmm, it was about Park Jaehyung.

751
00:39:15,854 --> 00:39:17,771
I guess you really can see the future.

752
00:39:17,772 --> 00:39:19,147
[Jiyun sighs]

753
00:39:19,148 --> 00:39:22,150
I can't believe the person I loved
was that messed up.

754
00:39:22,151 --> 00:39:24,945
[sighs deeply] I know how you feel.

755
00:39:24,946 --> 00:39:26,655
I always fall for the bad women.

756
00:39:26,656 --> 00:39:28,366
- I wonder why.
- [Jiyun scoffs softly]

757
00:39:29,367 --> 00:39:32,786
Actually, Waiter Hong!
Give us your most expensive whiskey.

758
00:39:32,787 --> 00:39:34,371
No, a drink to celebrate.

759
00:39:34,372 --> 00:39:36,123
Give us a bottle of champagne.

760
00:39:36,124 --> 00:39:37,249
[Jiyun scoffs softly]

761
00:39:37,250 --> 00:39:38,960
[♪ upbeat, jaunty music playing]

762
00:39:41,796 --> 00:39:43,171
Now,

763
00:39:43,172 --> 00:39:45,716
you're finally free
from that piece of trash,

764
00:39:45,717 --> 00:39:47,594
so here's to your new life.

765
00:39:48,595 --> 00:39:49,762
- [clinking]
- Cheers.

766
00:39:53,933 --> 00:39:55,059
Mmm.

767
00:39:55,393 --> 00:39:56,560
[sighs in exasperation]

768
00:39:56,561 --> 00:40:00,022
I really don't think I'll feel any better
until I punch that bastard.

769
00:40:00,023 --> 00:40:01,274
Mmm...

770
00:40:02,191 --> 00:40:04,027
[in English] Good idea.
[in Korean] I like it.

771
00:40:05,361 --> 00:40:06,613
Yes, cheers again.

772
00:40:07,196 --> 00:40:08,281
[clinking]

773
00:40:08,740 --> 00:40:10,157
[inhales sharply]

774
00:40:10,158 --> 00:40:11,408
[exhales softly]

775
00:40:11,409 --> 00:40:12,660
[♪ music fades]

776
00:40:13,620 --> 00:40:16,121
SEOUL GANGHA POLICE STATION

777
00:40:16,122 --> 00:40:18,373
Park Jaeha? I heard he's dead.

778
00:40:18,374 --> 00:40:19,917
What's a dead guy doing here?

779
00:40:19,918 --> 00:40:21,752
- Show us.
- Show us a magic trick.

780
00:40:21,753 --> 00:40:23,045
How can I do magic here?

781
00:40:23,046 --> 00:40:24,379
Do it.

782
00:40:24,380 --> 00:40:25,589
- Please stop.
- Do it.

783
00:40:25,590 --> 00:40:26,633
[Jaeha] Don't touch me.

784
00:40:27,759 --> 00:40:29,636
Oh, those guys are back again?

785
00:40:31,804 --> 00:40:33,598
- Did you need something?
- Ah.

786
00:40:34,474 --> 00:40:35,641
I need a word.

787
00:40:35,642 --> 00:40:37,518
[♪ quirky, suspenseful music playing]

788
00:40:40,313 --> 00:40:41,897
[whispering] We'll take
Park Jaeha out and...

789
00:40:41,898 --> 00:40:43,274
[continues indistinctly]

790
00:40:53,618 --> 00:40:54,868
Stop touching me.

791
00:40:54,869 --> 00:40:55,870
Do some magic for us.

792
00:40:58,081 --> 00:41:00,749
Mr. Park Jaeha,
you're being moved to jail. Come out.

793
00:41:00,750 --> 00:41:02,042
[chuckles in relief]

794
00:41:02,043 --> 00:41:03,670
- Show us before you go.
- Don't go.

795
00:41:07,840 --> 00:41:09,092
Go left.

796
00:41:09,759 --> 00:41:13,179
My God, you look terrible, Mr. Park.

797
00:41:13,888 --> 00:41:15,180
Come here.

798
00:41:15,181 --> 00:41:16,306
It's all right.

799
00:41:16,307 --> 00:41:18,267
[in English] Now, follow me.

800
00:41:22,855 --> 00:41:24,731
Oh! Oh...

801
00:41:24,732 --> 00:41:25,900
[♪ music fades]

802
00:41:27,151 --> 00:41:28,277
[chuckles nervously]

803
00:41:29,070 --> 00:41:31,071
[in Korean] Did you come to say goodbye?

804
00:41:31,072 --> 00:41:32,991
We couldn't just let you go.

805
00:41:34,367 --> 00:41:35,701
- You son of a bitch.
- What?

806
00:41:35,702 --> 00:41:36,952
[♪ quirky music playing]

807
00:41:36,953 --> 00:41:39,246
- You!
- You bastard! How could you?

808
00:41:39,247 --> 00:41:41,916
You shouldn't be doing this, ladies.
The stomach!

809
00:41:42,750 --> 00:41:45,377
- [officer] That's enough.
- [Dahee] Get out of the way.

810
00:41:45,378 --> 00:41:46,878
You bastard!

811
00:41:46,879 --> 00:41:48,171
[Jaeha] I...

812
00:41:48,172 --> 00:41:49,298
[Jiyun panting]

813
00:41:49,882 --> 00:41:51,217
I loved all of you.

814
00:41:54,846 --> 00:41:56,221
[exclaims]

815
00:41:56,222 --> 00:41:57,265
Shut your mouth.

816
00:41:58,224 --> 00:41:59,726
[Hyera] What's going on?

817
00:42:00,435 --> 00:42:03,353
Right. Isn't the transport van over there?

818
00:42:03,354 --> 00:42:04,688
I guess I was mistaken.

819
00:42:04,689 --> 00:42:06,189
What? It's at the front gate.

820
00:42:06,190 --> 00:42:08,025
It's the front gate. Ah, my mistake.

821
00:42:08,026 --> 00:42:09,109
Mistake?

822
00:42:09,110 --> 00:42:11,612
Yes, exactly. Nobody's perfect.

823
00:42:12,405 --> 00:42:13,865
Hey, take him away.

824
00:42:15,950 --> 00:42:17,576
[Jaeha] I really loved you.

825
00:42:17,577 --> 00:42:18,828
- I mean it.
- Bro.

826
00:42:19,996 --> 00:42:21,913
Well done. Time to go home.

827
00:42:21,914 --> 00:42:24,541
You've got a mean punch.
Ever thought about boxing?

828
00:42:24,542 --> 00:42:25,710
Jin Isoo.

829
00:42:26,335 --> 00:42:28,962
- Submit a written apology.
- A written apology.

830
00:42:28,963 --> 00:42:31,631
That's my specialty. You got it.

831
00:42:31,632 --> 00:42:33,593
- [scoffs]
- [♪ music fades]

832
00:42:38,765 --> 00:42:40,433
[sneezing]

833
00:42:42,310 --> 00:42:43,352
[door opens]

834
00:42:47,106 --> 00:42:48,356
[Jaeha sighs softly]

835
00:42:48,357 --> 00:42:50,734
[♪ gentle, wistful music playing]

836
00:42:50,735 --> 00:42:51,944
Sujeong.

837
00:43:08,419 --> 00:43:09,420
Sujeong.

838
00:43:10,463 --> 00:43:11,671
[chuckles]

839
00:43:11,672 --> 00:43:13,049
My Sujeong.

840
00:43:14,634 --> 00:43:16,010
You look beautiful today.

841
00:43:17,428 --> 00:43:19,388
Like a cherry blossom. [chuckling]

842
00:43:20,598 --> 00:43:21,849
[sighs softly]

843
00:43:23,184 --> 00:43:25,144
Did you come all the way here to see me?

844
00:43:26,854 --> 00:43:27,855
Jaeha.

845
00:43:28,898 --> 00:43:30,441
You'll be out of here soon.

846
00:43:31,359 --> 00:43:34,529
My dad hired a great lawyer.

847
00:43:40,493 --> 00:43:41,619
[exhales sharply]

848
00:43:43,704 --> 00:43:45,706
[voice shaking] I don't know
what I'd do without you.

849
00:43:48,960 --> 00:43:51,045
You were my first love.

850
00:43:53,381 --> 00:43:54,464
But...

851
00:43:54,465 --> 00:43:57,384
[inhales deeply, exhales]

852
00:43:57,385 --> 00:43:59,719
...my life feels meaningless now.

853
00:43:59,720 --> 00:44:00,888
[breath trembles]

854
00:44:03,766 --> 00:44:04,934
I'll make it up to you.

855
00:44:05,643 --> 00:44:06,811
From now on,

856
00:44:07,854 --> 00:44:09,438
I'll be really good to you.

857
00:44:11,274 --> 00:44:13,066
You should.

858
00:44:13,067 --> 00:44:15,694
I'll be spending every day
waiting for you to get out.

859
00:44:15,695 --> 00:44:16,863
[♪ music fades]

860
00:44:18,948 --> 00:44:20,116
Once you're out,

861
00:44:21,784 --> 00:44:23,577
I'm going to kill you myself.

862
00:44:23,578 --> 00:44:25,663
[♪ tense, foreboding music playing]

863
00:44:28,124 --> 00:44:29,208
[chuckling nervously]

864
00:44:32,420 --> 00:44:35,423
Why would you say
something so scary, Sujeong?

865
00:44:35,965 --> 00:44:38,884
Try running if you want.

866
00:44:38,885 --> 00:44:40,595
Wherever you hide,

867
00:44:41,554 --> 00:44:43,054
I'm going to find you.

868
00:44:43,055 --> 00:44:44,849
- [♪ music fades]
- What?

869
00:44:46,225 --> 00:44:48,101
All the best until then.

870
00:44:48,102 --> 00:44:49,394
[♪ quirky music playing]

871
00:44:49,395 --> 00:44:50,812
Wait, Sujeong.

872
00:44:50,813 --> 00:44:51,814
Sujeong!

873
00:44:52,732 --> 00:44:53,941
Sujeong, wait!

874
00:44:55,067 --> 00:44:56,860
You've suddenly changed!

875
00:44:56,861 --> 00:44:58,321
Why are you doing this to me?

876
00:44:59,197 --> 00:45:01,406
[voice shaking] If you do this too,
what am I supposed to do?

877
00:45:01,407 --> 00:45:02,575
[sobbing]

878
00:45:04,285 --> 00:45:05,369
[♪ music fades]

879
00:45:11,125 --> 00:45:12,668
[line ringing over car speaker]

880
00:45:13,711 --> 00:45:16,463
[automated voice] <i>The number
you have dialed is unavailable.</i>

881
00:45:16,464 --> 00:45:18,424
Why isn't he picking up?

882
00:45:19,425 --> 00:45:21,385
MR. CHOI

883
00:45:22,720 --> 00:45:24,680
[line connects, ringing]

884
00:45:26,182 --> 00:45:28,351
<i>- Yes, Detective Jin.</i>
- Hi, Mr. Kim.

885
00:45:29,018 --> 00:45:32,270
I can't seem to reach the chairman lately.
Is he very busy?

886
00:45:32,271 --> 00:45:33,898
<i>He's on vacation.</i>

887
00:45:34,982 --> 00:45:37,359
- Vacation?
<i>- He didn't say he was traveling.</i>

888
00:45:37,360 --> 00:45:39,527
<i>- Shall I call him for you?</i>
- No, it's fine.

889
00:45:39,528 --> 00:45:41,821
He'll be reading books at home, then.

890
00:45:41,822 --> 00:45:44,241
That's his idea of a vacation.
I'll go to his house.

891
00:45:44,242 --> 00:45:45,534
[engine revving]

892
00:45:52,541 --> 00:45:53,876
[doorbell chimes]

893
00:45:55,920 --> 00:45:57,296
[doorbell chimes]

894
00:45:58,798 --> 00:45:59,799
What on earth?

895
00:46:01,133 --> 00:46:02,801
- [door unlocks]
- [digital lock beeps]

896
00:46:02,802 --> 00:46:05,053
- [door closes]
- Mr. Choi, it's me!

897
00:46:05,054 --> 00:46:06,097
[digital lock beeps]

898
00:46:08,057 --> 00:46:09,183
Mr. Choi!

899
00:46:12,228 --> 00:46:13,896
PRE AND POST STOMACH CANCER SURGERY

900
00:46:20,319 --> 00:46:21,653
PRE-SURGERY PREPARATION

901
00:46:21,654 --> 00:46:22,905
[♪ gentle, melancholy music playing]

902
00:46:23,781 --> 00:46:25,992
ADMISSION INFORMATION

903
00:46:36,210 --> 00:46:37,336
[sighs softly]

904
00:46:46,887 --> 00:46:48,263
What are you doing here?

905
00:46:48,264 --> 00:46:49,557
Detective Jin.

906
00:46:53,269 --> 00:46:54,979
I asked, what are you doing?

907
00:46:55,646 --> 00:46:57,023
How did you know I was here?

908
00:47:00,026 --> 00:47:01,192
[Isoo sighs]

909
00:47:01,193 --> 00:47:02,653
Were you never going to tell me?

910
00:47:03,529 --> 00:47:05,447
It's not a serious illness.

911
00:47:05,448 --> 00:47:07,116
And the surgery went well.

912
00:47:09,577 --> 00:47:12,121
I thought of you as family.

913
00:47:13,456 --> 00:47:15,374
But it looks like I meant nothing to you.

914
00:47:16,208 --> 00:47:18,210
I just didn't want to bother you.

915
00:47:19,920 --> 00:47:21,004
Did I scare you?

916
00:47:21,005 --> 00:47:22,006
[sighs softly]

917
00:47:23,007 --> 00:47:25,258
In my recent case,

918
00:47:25,259 --> 00:47:27,345
a terminal cancer patient
took his own life.

919
00:47:28,554 --> 00:47:30,431
But then I hear that you have cancer.

920
00:47:32,516 --> 00:47:33,726
[sighs heavily]

921
00:47:35,728 --> 00:47:36,771
I'm sorry.

922
00:47:37,688 --> 00:47:38,689
[Isoo sighs softly]

923
00:47:39,774 --> 00:47:40,775
[♪ music fades]

924
00:47:46,447 --> 00:47:47,490
[Isoo sighs]

925
00:47:49,325 --> 00:47:51,409
Why is your hospital room so shabby?

926
00:47:51,410 --> 00:47:54,788
It's not shabby at all.
It's a perfectly nice room.

927
00:47:54,789 --> 00:47:56,331
You don't even have any flowers.

928
00:47:56,332 --> 00:47:58,584
I don't need flowers at my age. [chuckles]

929
00:47:59,418 --> 00:48:01,127
And your clothes are all wet.

930
00:48:01,128 --> 00:48:03,088
How are you going to get changed, huh?

931
00:48:03,089 --> 00:48:05,757
As if you'd bother me.
Take it off and change.

932
00:48:05,758 --> 00:48:08,551
I'll do it myself later.

933
00:48:08,552 --> 00:48:10,136
[inhales sharply] Take it off.
You need to change!

934
00:48:10,137 --> 00:48:11,388
Uh... [exhales]

935
00:48:11,389 --> 00:48:13,223
[♪ gentle, poignant music playing]

936
00:48:13,224 --> 00:48:14,308
[grunts softly]

937
00:48:18,896 --> 00:48:20,648
GET WELL SOON

938
00:48:21,273 --> 00:48:22,274
Thank you.

939
00:48:25,820 --> 00:48:26,946
[door opens]

940
00:48:28,447 --> 00:48:29,490
[door closes]

941
00:48:32,701 --> 00:48:33,911
[sneezes]

942
00:48:36,997 --> 00:48:38,457
Whoa!

943
00:48:39,708 --> 00:48:41,584
- Looks like someone was here.
- [coughs]

944
00:48:41,585 --> 00:48:42,670
Yes.

945
00:48:43,212 --> 00:48:45,255
Someone I think of as a son stopped by.

946
00:48:45,256 --> 00:48:46,673
[chuckles]

947
00:48:46,674 --> 00:48:49,217
The scent's quite strong.

948
00:48:49,218 --> 00:48:51,094
It is. [sneezes]

949
00:48:51,095 --> 00:48:52,303
[chuckling]

950
00:48:52,304 --> 00:48:53,930
[exhales sharply]

951
00:48:53,931 --> 00:48:55,598
[panting]

952
00:48:55,599 --> 00:48:56,642
[♪ music fades]

953
00:49:00,146 --> 00:49:01,313
[cell phone vibrating]

954
00:49:05,109 --> 00:49:06,110
Hey, babe.

955
00:49:06,944 --> 00:49:07,945
[Kyungjin gasps]

956
00:49:08,404 --> 00:49:09,487
[whispering] Shoot, I forgot.

957
00:49:09,488 --> 00:49:12,324
Okay, I'll be right there. Sorry.

958
00:49:13,409 --> 00:49:14,410
[line disconnects]

959
00:49:15,119 --> 00:49:17,370
Hey, where are you going?

960
00:49:17,371 --> 00:49:18,663
To see my girlfriend.

961
00:49:18,664 --> 00:49:20,790
We're supposed to hang out today.

962
00:49:20,791 --> 00:49:23,585
I forgot I had a date. Sorry, bro!

963
00:49:23,586 --> 00:49:24,837
Hey!

964
00:49:25,713 --> 00:49:27,005
[sighs]

965
00:49:27,006 --> 00:49:29,090
He's completely whipped by his girlfriend.

966
00:49:29,091 --> 00:49:30,968
- [sighs in exasperation]
- [cell phone vibrating]

967
00:49:35,306 --> 00:49:36,765
Hi, Jiwon.

968
00:49:38,058 --> 00:49:39,934
What? Where are you?

969
00:49:39,935 --> 00:49:42,353
I'll be right there. I won't be long.

970
00:49:42,354 --> 00:49:43,938
- [line disconnects]
- Hey, what's going on?

971
00:49:43,939 --> 00:49:45,148
Jiwon hurt herself.

972
00:49:45,149 --> 00:49:46,858
I need to go. Sorry. Bye.

973
00:49:46,859 --> 00:49:47,942
Hey, you're...

974
00:49:47,943 --> 00:49:49,069
[♪ quirky music playing]

975
00:49:50,488 --> 00:49:52,031
He's the one who's whipped.

976
00:49:53,157 --> 00:49:54,617
[exhales incredulously]

977
00:49:56,202 --> 00:49:57,286
[clicks tongue]

978
00:50:00,915 --> 00:50:02,333
[line connects, ringing]

979
00:50:04,502 --> 00:50:06,961
- [line clicks]
- Hello? Yes, it's me.

980
00:50:06,962 --> 00:50:10,841
I can't make it today,
so I'll have to cancel.

981
00:50:11,759 --> 00:50:12,967
[line disconnects]

982
00:50:12,968 --> 00:50:16,054
Where is everyone? I thought
you were having a guys-only party.

983
00:50:16,055 --> 00:50:17,473
They betrayed me.

984
00:50:19,433 --> 00:50:20,809
[keyboard clacking]

985
00:50:22,561 --> 00:50:23,729
[♪ music fades]

986
00:50:27,441 --> 00:50:28,442
Jiwon.

987
00:50:29,026 --> 00:50:31,987
[panting] What happened?
Are you badly hurt?

988
00:50:32,780 --> 00:50:34,113
No. [sighs]

989
00:50:34,114 --> 00:50:36,825
I was trying to get back into running
and pulled something.

990
00:50:38,369 --> 00:50:40,329
I think it might be broken.

991
00:50:41,330 --> 00:50:42,456
[sighs heavily]

992
00:50:43,582 --> 00:50:45,251
Let's go to the hospital. Hop on.

993
00:50:48,087 --> 00:50:51,381
[chuckles] I'm joking. Honestly.

994
00:50:51,382 --> 00:50:52,675
Sit here.

995
00:50:54,677 --> 00:50:56,554
Are you sure you're okay?

996
00:50:57,221 --> 00:50:58,222
[Dr. Yoon] Mmm.

997
00:50:59,056 --> 00:51:00,223
[♪ gentle, tender music playing]

998
00:51:00,224 --> 00:51:01,809
[both chuckle]

999
00:51:02,726 --> 00:51:04,687
[clears throat] Right now...

1000
00:51:07,147 --> 00:51:10,568
[sighs] ...I just need some comforting.

1001
00:51:20,327 --> 00:51:21,537
[Dr. Yoon chuckles]

1002
00:51:22,871 --> 00:51:24,081
[♪ music fades]

1003
00:51:26,667 --> 00:51:27,792
[Kyungjin] This looks gorgeous.

1004
00:51:27,793 --> 00:51:29,627
[♪ soft ambient music
playing in background]

1005
00:51:29,628 --> 00:51:31,337
Hey, what are you doing?

1006
00:51:31,338 --> 00:51:33,715
Hey, leave this to me.

1007
00:51:33,716 --> 00:51:37,720
I didn't do anything for you on White Day.
You don't have to lift a finger today.

1008
00:51:40,806 --> 00:51:42,682
Here, open up.

1009
00:51:42,683 --> 00:51:44,392
Leave it. I'll eat it myself.

1010
00:51:44,393 --> 00:51:46,645
- I'm going to eat it.
- [scoffs]

1011
00:51:47,479 --> 00:51:48,480
Whoa!

1012
00:51:48,772 --> 00:51:49,773
It's delicious!

1013
00:51:52,776 --> 00:51:53,777
Mmm!

1014
00:51:58,782 --> 00:52:00,658
It's good, right? Wow!

1015
00:52:00,659 --> 00:52:03,037
Isoo's recommendations never disappoint.

1016
00:52:04,955 --> 00:52:07,332
Babe, you know
we caught Park Jaeha, right?

1017
00:52:07,333 --> 00:52:08,958
Do you know how we did it?

1018
00:52:08,959 --> 00:52:11,210
Sometimes I really think Isoo is a genius.

1019
00:52:11,211 --> 00:52:12,713
- [fork clatters on table]
- No, he is a genius.

1020
00:52:14,840 --> 00:52:16,341
We should break up.

1021
00:52:16,342 --> 00:52:17,343
What?

1022
00:52:18,260 --> 00:52:19,385
What did you just say?

1023
00:52:19,386 --> 00:52:20,970
I want to break up.

1024
00:52:20,971 --> 00:52:22,681
[♪ quirky, dramatic music playing]

1025
00:52:23,766 --> 00:52:25,933
You're breaking up with me over <i>tonkatsu?</i>

1026
00:52:25,934 --> 00:52:27,770
Don't you know why I want to break up?

1027
00:52:28,437 --> 00:52:30,104
I'm asking because I don't.

1028
00:52:30,105 --> 00:52:33,274
[scoffs] Forget it. What more
can I possibly say to you?

1029
00:52:33,275 --> 00:52:34,818
I'm leaving.

1030
00:52:47,998 --> 00:52:50,750
Excuse me. Can you
box up this <i>tonkatsu</i> for me?

1031
00:52:50,751 --> 00:52:53,336
Wow. You're getting it to go right now?

1032
00:52:53,337 --> 00:52:56,256
Hey, the <i>tonkatsu</i> did nothing wrong.

1033
00:52:59,218 --> 00:53:00,635
But still...

1034
00:53:00,636 --> 00:53:01,929
Thank you.

1035
00:53:02,513 --> 00:53:03,971
Uh...

1036
00:53:03,972 --> 00:53:06,934
Have a good life, with your beloved Isoo.

1037
00:53:08,936 --> 00:53:09,937
Bye.

1038
00:53:12,398 --> 00:53:13,649
Wow!

1039
00:53:14,608 --> 00:53:15,651
[scoffs]

1040
00:53:16,151 --> 00:53:17,361
[chuckling]

1041
00:53:19,988 --> 00:53:21,657
- It's still delicious.
- [♪ music fades]

1042
00:53:24,159 --> 00:53:26,869
[sighs wearily] Story of my life.

1043
00:53:26,870 --> 00:53:28,788
Stabbed in the back by guys.

1044
00:53:28,789 --> 00:53:30,040
Time to go home!

1045
00:53:31,417 --> 00:53:33,377
Want to get a drink with me?

1046
00:53:39,883 --> 00:53:40,967
- [Isoo] Cheers.
- [clink]

1047
00:53:40,968 --> 00:53:42,343
[♪ soft jazz music playing in background]

1048
00:53:42,344 --> 00:53:43,387
[slurps]

1049
00:53:43,846 --> 00:53:44,971
[exhales contentedly]

1050
00:53:44,972 --> 00:53:47,391
How's the aroma, huh? Amazing, isn't it?

1051
00:53:48,142 --> 00:53:49,225
[sniffs]

1052
00:53:49,226 --> 00:53:50,518
Yeah, it's amazing.

1053
00:53:50,519 --> 00:53:55,440
[sighs smugly] I spent eight whole months
trying everything to nail this flavor.

1054
00:53:55,441 --> 00:53:57,024
[exhales incredulously]

1055
00:53:57,025 --> 00:53:59,111
I drink soju and beer,
so I can't really tell.

1056
00:53:59,695 --> 00:54:01,571
Oh, you've got no taste.

1057
00:54:01,572 --> 00:54:04,449
Want to try something new?
You can try whiskey starting today.

1058
00:54:04,450 --> 00:54:06,952
No, I'm good. [chuckles]

1059
00:54:07,536 --> 00:54:08,704
[Hyera inhales sharply]

1060
00:54:09,413 --> 00:54:11,456
You even know how to make whiskey.

1061
00:54:11,457 --> 00:54:13,833
You're full of surprises, Jin Isoo.

1062
00:54:13,834 --> 00:54:15,543
What's the matter with you?

1063
00:54:15,544 --> 00:54:19,130
Did another soul fall for my charms? Huh?

1064
00:54:19,131 --> 00:54:20,674
[scoffs, chuckles]

1065
00:54:21,467 --> 00:54:22,468
That said,

1066
00:54:23,802 --> 00:54:26,971
as a cop, you're undeniably
walking a fine line.

1067
00:54:26,972 --> 00:54:28,848
You'll fall if you're not careful.

1068
00:54:28,849 --> 00:54:30,016
Don't worry.

1069
00:54:30,017 --> 00:54:32,643
I was born in the Year of the Monkey.
I'm good at keeping balance.

1070
00:54:32,644 --> 00:54:33,645
[chuckles]

1071
00:54:34,646 --> 00:54:36,689
You just need to use me.

1072
00:54:36,690 --> 00:54:38,566
I'll do anything you need.

1073
00:54:38,567 --> 00:54:40,693
As the cheat code to solving cases.

1074
00:54:40,694 --> 00:54:42,321
Right, cheat code.

1075
00:54:43,530 --> 00:54:44,615
[clink]

1076
00:54:46,158 --> 00:54:47,284
[Isoo exhales softly]

1077
00:54:48,035 --> 00:54:51,205
Will you return to Hansu Group one day?

1078
00:54:51,788 --> 00:54:53,664
Mmm... The truth is...

1079
00:54:53,665 --> 00:54:54,791
[inhales deeply]

1080
00:54:55,501 --> 00:54:57,669
...I dumped it all on Mr. Choi
and ran away.

1081
00:54:58,795 --> 00:55:02,174
He's like an uncle and a father to me,

1082
00:55:03,759 --> 00:55:06,344
but now I'm worried
I put too much on his shoulders.

1083
00:55:06,345 --> 00:55:07,471
[Isoo] Hmm.

1084
00:55:10,224 --> 00:55:11,308
By the way,

1085
00:55:12,392 --> 00:55:15,311
why did you return to Gangha?

1086
00:55:15,312 --> 00:55:17,606
It's odd. You were
doing great at Counterterrorism.

1087
00:55:19,566 --> 00:55:21,276
I have someone I need to catch.

1088
00:55:22,736 --> 00:55:23,779
Who?

1089
00:55:25,280 --> 00:55:27,074
Tell me, we can catch them together.

1090
00:55:30,494 --> 00:55:31,869
Yu Seongwon.

1091
00:55:31,870 --> 00:55:33,829
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

1092
00:55:33,830 --> 00:55:34,831
Yu Seongwon?

1093
00:55:38,126 --> 00:55:40,336
The Yu Seongwon I know?

1094
00:55:40,337 --> 00:55:41,338
Yes.

1095
00:55:43,465 --> 00:55:45,217
What did he do?

1096
00:55:48,637 --> 00:55:49,680
Serial killings.

1097
00:56:01,149 --> 00:56:02,233
Where is Seongwon?

1098
00:56:02,234 --> 00:56:03,944
At his studio.

1099
00:56:05,654 --> 00:56:06,655
Let's go.

1100
00:56:13,745 --> 00:56:15,330
[♪ suspenseful music continues]

1101
00:56:39,980 --> 00:56:41,148
Chairwoman.

1102
00:56:43,900 --> 00:56:45,735
What brings you all the way here?

1103
00:56:45,736 --> 00:56:47,486
When are you leaving?

1104
00:56:47,487 --> 00:56:48,904
Uh...

1105
00:56:48,905 --> 00:56:51,490
I'm not sure.
I have another exhibition coming up.

1106
00:56:51,491 --> 00:56:52,743
Cancel it and leave.

1107
00:56:53,535 --> 00:56:55,078
That's going to be a problem.

1108
00:56:55,996 --> 00:56:57,789
You see, I can't return to the UK.

1109
00:57:00,876 --> 00:57:01,960
Wow!

1110
00:57:02,836 --> 00:57:04,670
That's a great expression.

1111
00:57:04,671 --> 00:57:06,048
[♪ music increases in tempo]

1112
00:57:06,715 --> 00:57:08,425
Makes me want to sculpt it.

1113
00:57:09,551 --> 00:57:10,594
Wherever it is...

1114
00:57:17,476 --> 00:57:19,686
just pack up and leave quickly.

1115
00:57:22,689 --> 00:57:23,690
Why?

1116
00:57:24,816 --> 00:57:27,985
Do you find it unbearable
that I'm so much like you, Mom?

1117
00:57:27,986 --> 00:57:29,111
[♪ music resumes tempo]

1118
00:57:29,112 --> 00:57:30,321
You know it's true.

1119
00:57:30,322 --> 00:57:32,156
You killed Dad.

1120
00:57:32,157 --> 00:57:33,240
And I...

1121
00:57:33,241 --> 00:57:34,993
uh, wonder...

1122
00:57:35,869 --> 00:57:37,537
[sings] who I killed.

1123
00:57:42,334 --> 00:57:43,584
[chuckles]

1124
00:57:43,585 --> 00:57:46,337
You want to lock me up
in a psych ward again, don't you?

1125
00:57:46,338 --> 00:57:48,674
Because I'm your Achilles' heel.

1126
00:57:49,841 --> 00:57:50,842
But...

1127
00:57:51,843 --> 00:57:53,804
that's not going to happen.

1128
00:57:54,596 --> 00:57:57,598
Your son is famous now.

1129
00:57:57,599 --> 00:57:59,226
[♪ music increases in tempo]

1130
00:58:17,411 --> 00:58:18,495
Leaving so soon?

1131
00:58:19,621 --> 00:58:21,914
Not even a hug
after being apart for four years?

1132
00:58:21,915 --> 00:58:23,750
Are you scared of me?

1133
00:58:24,960 --> 00:58:26,545
- And you call yourself a mother?
- [♪ music swells]

1134
00:58:28,130 --> 00:58:29,715
[♪ music resumes tempo]

1135
00:58:46,148 --> 00:58:47,149
Keep an eye on him

1136
00:58:48,358 --> 00:58:50,276
so he doesn't cause any trouble.

1137
00:58:50,277 --> 00:58:51,444
Yes, ma'am.

1138
00:58:51,445 --> 00:58:53,446
Call me if anything happens.

1139
00:58:53,447 --> 00:58:54,655
Yes, ma'am.

1140
00:58:54,656 --> 00:58:55,948
[♪ tense, pulsating music playing]

1141
00:58:55,949 --> 00:58:57,284
Mr. Hwang.

1142
00:59:06,877 --> 00:59:08,086
I'm counting on you.

1143
00:59:09,337 --> 00:59:10,630
Yes, understood, ma'am.

1144
00:59:22,142 --> 00:59:23,143
[car engine starts]

1145
00:59:27,022 --> 00:59:28,273
[♪ music fades]

1146
00:59:30,734 --> 00:59:32,944
[♪ gentle piano music
playing in background]

1147
00:59:48,251 --> 00:59:49,294
She's beautiful.

1148
00:59:49,961 --> 00:59:51,212
[chuckles softly]

1149
00:59:51,213 --> 00:59:52,255
[bartender] Who is she?

1150
00:59:53,381 --> 00:59:55,049
Someone who's obsessed with me.

1151
00:59:55,050 --> 00:59:56,051
[chuckles softly]

1152
00:59:56,635 --> 00:59:57,636
Is she a stalker?

1153
00:59:58,470 --> 01:00:00,179
You could say that.

1154
01:00:00,180 --> 01:00:03,266
I'm wondering if I should make her
the model for my next sculpture.

1155
01:00:05,060 --> 01:00:07,145
You're the sculptor, Yu Seongwon, right?

1156
01:00:09,147 --> 01:00:10,524
I went to your exhibition.

1157
01:00:14,861 --> 01:00:16,071
How was it?

1158
01:00:18,281 --> 01:00:19,282
Uh...

1159
01:00:20,784 --> 01:00:23,536
When I was looking at your pieces,

1160
01:00:23,537 --> 01:00:25,413
I almost felt like I couldn't breathe.

1161
01:00:26,414 --> 01:00:27,498
[chuckles softly]

1162
01:00:27,499 --> 01:00:30,502
I felt overwhelmed, I guess.

1163
01:00:31,127 --> 01:00:32,921
[chuckles] You flatter me.

1164
01:00:34,047 --> 01:00:37,425
It felt like there was
some hidden meaning behind it.

1165
01:00:39,553 --> 01:00:41,471
It's all out in the open,

1166
01:00:42,138 --> 01:00:44,099
but not quite revealing the truth.

1167
01:00:45,892 --> 01:00:47,018
You're very perceptive.

1168
01:00:48,395 --> 01:00:50,230
I used to study art.

1169
01:00:51,398 --> 01:00:53,108
I'm taking a break to work.

1170
01:00:53,817 --> 01:00:55,235
Why did you take a break?

1171
01:00:57,988 --> 01:01:00,365
Let's just say, no comment.

1172
01:01:02,909 --> 01:01:06,079
[Hyera] Four years ago,
two of Yu Seongwon's models disappeared.

1173
01:01:06,788 --> 01:01:08,498
And one of his underclassmen.

1174
01:01:09,291 --> 01:01:11,542
They were all closed
as missing persons cases,

1175
01:01:11,543 --> 01:01:14,461
but I think Yu Seongwon killed them.

1176
01:01:14,462 --> 01:01:16,006
[♪ ominous music playing]

1177
01:01:18,508 --> 01:01:19,801
What do you think?

1178
01:01:21,511 --> 01:01:23,179
Is the Yu Seongwon you know

1179
01:01:24,097 --> 01:01:25,473
capable of killing people?

1180
01:01:28,810 --> 01:01:31,187
No, the Seongwon I know

1181
01:01:32,814 --> 01:01:34,858
is timid and soft-hearted.

1182
01:01:36,401 --> 01:01:37,944
Do you have any evidence?

1183
01:01:39,070 --> 01:01:40,779
No, just my gut feeling.

1184
01:01:40,780 --> 01:01:42,615
His alibi checked out.

1185
01:01:42,616 --> 01:01:44,450
[♪ melancholy piano music playing]

1186
01:01:44,451 --> 01:01:45,911
Then it might not be him.

1187
01:01:47,329 --> 01:01:49,789
I was contacted by the UK police recently.

1188
01:01:51,666 --> 01:01:54,961
Two of Yu Seongwon's models are missing.

1189
01:02:04,971 --> 01:02:08,140
I have to submit a piece
for a contemporary art exhibition,

1190
01:02:08,141 --> 01:02:09,892
but I can't seem to find a model.

1191
01:02:09,893 --> 01:02:12,686
Shall I introduce you to someone?

1192
01:02:12,687 --> 01:02:14,897
[♪ tense, foreboding music playing]

1193
01:02:14,898 --> 01:02:16,274
SONG AREUM

1194
01:02:19,778 --> 01:02:21,655
How about you, Areum?

1195
01:02:31,831 --> 01:02:32,999
Would you

1196
01:02:34,167 --> 01:02:35,626
be my model?

1197
01:02:35,627 --> 01:02:37,045
[♪ music swells]

1198
01:02:48,932 --> 01:02:50,015
FLEX X COP 2
EPISODE 8

1199
01:02:50,016 --> 01:02:51,600
THE TRUTH ABOUT YU SEONGWON COMES TO LIGHT

1200
01:02:51,601 --> 01:02:53,603
[♪ upbeat pop music playing]

1201
01:03:09,119 --> 01:03:12,621
Special Cast. Son Woohyeon

1202
01:03:12,622 --> 01:03:16,125
Special Cast. Jung Chaeyeon

1203
01:03:16,126 --> 01:03:19,546
Special Cast. Heo Sungtae

1204
01:03:30,640 --> 01:03:32,266
- [all scream]
- [Hyera] <i>Who is the deceased student?</i>

1205
01:03:32,267 --> 01:03:35,310
Murder? No student
at our school would do that.

1206
01:03:35,311 --> 01:03:37,312
Was Seyeon alone yesterday?

1207
01:03:37,313 --> 01:03:39,732
[student 1] <i>The principal
supervised her personally.</i>

1208
01:03:39,733 --> 01:03:42,401
- Moon Seyeon's death was a curse.
- A curse?

1209
01:03:42,402 --> 01:03:44,028
Wait, I'll buy you cream puffs!

1210
01:03:44,029 --> 01:03:45,487
<i>We have to focus on the curse.</i>

1211
01:03:45,488 --> 01:03:46,739
[student 2] <i>It's from the Witch Shop.</i>

1212
01:03:46,740 --> 01:03:48,699
- Who do you want to curse?
- The police.

1213
01:03:48,700 --> 01:03:49,825
Why would the police...

1214
01:03:49,826 --> 01:03:52,369
[Hyera] <i>Someone hated Moon Seyeon.</i>

1215
01:03:52,370 --> 01:03:54,163
- [student 3] <i>A senior died last year.</i>
- A ghost?

1216
01:03:54,164 --> 01:03:55,330
Stay back!

1217
01:03:55,331 --> 01:03:56,790
- [Kyungjin] <i>The CCTVs?
-</i> [man] <i>They were down.</i>

1218
01:03:56,791 --> 01:03:58,293
It makes no sense.

1219
01:03:58,960 --> 01:04:00,669
They're still at the school.

1220
01:04:00,670 --> 01:04:01,754
[both gasp]

1221
01:04:01,755 --> 01:04:04,423
Be careful. Someone's after you.

1222
01:04:04,424 --> 01:04:05,507
That's a secret.

1223
01:04:05,508 --> 01:04:08,011
[woman] <i>I have a bad feeling about this.</i>

1224
01:04:14,517 --> 01:04:16,894
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

1225
01:04:16,895 --> 01:04:18,646
CONTACT ANALYSIS: YU SEONGWON

1226
01:04:21,900 --> 01:04:24,819
VICTIM 3: KIM HEEJUN
MISSING SINCE 16 SEP 2021

1227
01:04:33,161 --> 01:04:34,537
[cell phone vibrating]

1228
01:04:41,586 --> 01:04:43,630
[in English] Yes, this is Joo Hyera.

1229
01:04:45,006 --> 01:04:46,966
Yes, I requested the file.

1230
01:04:49,636 --> 01:04:50,928
Two people.

1231
01:04:50,929 --> 01:04:52,263
Are they missing?

1232
01:04:55,475 --> 01:04:56,476
Right.

1233
01:04:57,769 --> 01:04:59,562
I understand. Thank you.

1234
01:05:03,733 --> 01:05:04,818
[line disconnects]

1235
01:05:07,153 --> 01:05:08,321
[sighs wearily]

1236
01:05:18,832 --> 01:05:20,834
Translated by Hyesoo Lee
